1
00:00:00,087 --> 00:00:01,047
They stuck a needle

2
00:00:01,087 --> 00:00:02,370
into the dead spider—

3
00:00:02,410 --> 00:00:04,118
and its legs opened.

4
00:00:04,158 --> 00:00:05,807
You see, spiders use pressure

5
00:00:05,847 --> 00:00:06,567
inside their bodies

6
00:00:06,607 --> 00:00:08,074
to extend their legs.

7
00:00:08,114 --> 00:00:08,954
When they die,

8
00:00:08,994 --> 00:00:10,030
that pressure drops,

9
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:12,180
causing the legs to curl inward.

10
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,007
But researchers found

11
00:00:13,047 --> 00:00:14,447
they could push air through the needle

12
00:00:14,487 --> 00:00:15,994
to spread them open again.

13
00:00:16,034 --> 00:00:17,460
And when they released the pressure,

14
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:18,527
the legs snapped shut

15
00:00:18,567 --> 00:00:19,807
around an object.

16
00:00:19,847 --> 00:00:21,807
This turned the spider’s body into a claw

17
00:00:21,847 --> 00:00:23,860
that could lift more than its own weight.

18
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,754
They even made it reach down…

19
00:00:25,794 --> 00:00:27,287
and pick up another spider.

